From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau/gm20b: Keep idle timeout disabled during bundle init

Golden-context generation restores FE_GO_IDLE_TIMEOUT before injecting
the initialization bundles. On a Tegra210 Nano, intermittent frontend
INJECTED_BUNDLE_ERROR traps occur during this injection while the timeout
is enabled.

Keep the timeout disabled through bundle injection and wait for GR to
become idle before restoring it, following the NVIDIA Tegra driver's
initialization sequence.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/gr/ctxgm20b.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/engine/gr/ctxgm20b.c
@@ -58,13 +58,12 @@ gm20b_grctx_generate_main(struct gf100_gr_chan *chan)
 
 	gf100_gr_wait_idle(gr);
 
-	nvkm_wr32(device, 0x404154, idle_timeout);
-	gf100_gr_wait_idle(gr);
-
 	gf100_gr_mthd(gr, gr->method);
 	gf100_gr_wait_idle(gr);
 
 	gf100_gr_icmd(gr, gr->bundle);
+	gf100_gr_wait_idle(gr);
+	nvkm_wr32(device, 0x404154, idle_timeout);
 	grctx->pagepool(chan, chan->pagepool->addr);
 	grctx->bundle(chan, chan->bundle_cb->addr, grctx->bundle_size);
 }
